    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i know i should reach out but i just dont have the energy to explain it all over again to someone. it's like... every time i try to move forward, i just realize i'm moving away from the only time i actually felt alive. i look at his side of the bed and it just feels like the world ended and i'm just a ghost wandering around a house that doesn't belong to me anymore. it's so hard to see a \"future\" when my whole world was in that person. everything just feels so empty.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The ache of that emptiness is so deep, and it makes perfect sense that the thought of moving forward feels like betraying the beautiful moments you shared. It's not about forgetting; it's about learning how to carry the memory without letting it consume everything else. Sometimes, the most gentle way to start is by letting yourself feel the weight of the loss without the pressure to fix it right now.",
      "source": "target",
